### ProxyBans service — runnable request collection.
### Works in IntelliJ IDEA and in VS Code with the REST Client extension.
### Start the stack first: docker compose up --build

@host = http://localhost:8080
@token = dev-local-token
@player = 11111111-2222-3333-4444-555555555555
@admin = 99999999-8888-7777-6666-555555555555

### Health — the only endpoint that needs no token
GET {{host}}/actuator/health

### Register a player so names can be resolved (local mode only)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/known-players
X-Service-Token: {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "uuid": "{{player}}",
  "login": "Steve"
}

### Resolve a name to a UUID
GET {{host}}/api/v1/lookup?name=steve
X-Service-Token: {{token}}

### Issue a permanent ban
POST {{host}}/api/v1/bans
X-Service-Token: {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "playerUuid": "{{player}}",
  "issuedByUuid": "{{admin}}",
  "issuedByName": "Admin",
  "reason": "griefing spawn"
}

### Issue a 7-day ban
POST {{host}}/api/v1/bans
X-Service-Token: {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "playerUuid": "{{player}}",
  "issuedByUuid": "{{admin}}",
  "issuedByName": "Admin",
  "reason": "chat abuse",
  "durationSeconds": 604800
}

### The ban currently in force (404 when the player is clean)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/bans/{{player}}/active
X-Service-Token: {{token}}

### Active bans, newest first
GET {{host}}/api/v1/bans?limit=20&offset=0
X-Service-Token: {{token}}

### Punishment history
GET {{host}}/api/v1/bans/{{player}}/history?limit=20&offset=0
X-Service-Token: {{token}}

### Lift the ban
DELETE {{host}}/api/v1/bans/{{player}}
X-Service-Token: {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "liftedByUuid": "{{admin}}",
  "liftedByName": "Admin",
  "reason": "appeal accepted"
}

### Rejected: no token
GET {{host}}/api/v1/bans/{{player}}/active

### Rejected: limit above the maximum
GET {{host}}/api/v1/bans?limit=1000000
X-Service-Token: {{token}}
